# Input to `make runtime-lock`, which resolves it into requirements.lock with
# every version pinned and every distribution's SHA256 (ADR-0007, amended
# v0.8.4). The image installs only the lock, with --require-hashes; this file
# is never installed directly.
#
# pyarrow and Pillow take a floor: both ship fixes only in their newest line,
# so a ~= pin could never take one (CVE-2026-111497 in Arrow's bundled Brotli;
# CVE-2026-25990, fixed in Pillow 12.1.1). The rest stay on their major line.
# A floor here moves nothing by itself: a new version reaches the image only
# when the lock is regenerated, reviewed and released.
duckdb~=1.1
pandas~=2.2
polars~=1.8
pyarrow>=18.0
matplotlib~=3.10
Pillow>=12.1.1
